        "name": "USN-9165-1",
        "description": "Several security issues were discovered in the Linux kernel. An attacker could possibly use these to compromise the system. This update corrects flaws in the following subsystems:   - Cryptographic API;   - File systems infrastructure;   - Key management;   - Key Management;   - io_uring subsystem;   - PID namespace;   - Tracing infrastructure; (CVE-2026-99218, CVE-2026-99219, CVE-2026-99220, CVE-2026-99221, CVE-2026-99222, CVE-2026-99223, CVE-2026-99224, CVE-2026-99225, CVE-2026-99226, CVE-2026-99227, CVE-2026-99232, CVE-2026-99233, CVE-2026-99234, CVE-2026-99235, CVE-2026-99236, CVE-2026-99237, CVE-2026-99238, CVE-2026-99244, CVE-2026-99245)",
